  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through Monday)\nIssued at 1034 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nCloud cover begins to scatter out Tuesday night and Wednesday with\nwesterly winds and afternoon temperatures in the 60s/low 70s\nWednesday afternoon. \n\nAnother shortwave is progged to drop southeast into the region\nWednesday night and Thursday with a weak cold front into the CWA.\nWeak southerly low level winds return just ahead of this \ndisturbance, which will allow for a window of moisture advection\nback into the CWA Thursday. In response, low rain chances return\nacross northeast Oklahoma and northwest Arkansas Thursday. Latest\nmodel solutions show this shortwave exiting Thursday night. In the\nwake of this wave, more seasonal average temperatures are\nanticipated Friday into the weekend.",
